1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:05,422
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:08,216 --> 00:00:09,718
<i>You wanted to speak with me?</i>

3
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:13,221
<i>Billy, sorry.</i>

4
00:00:13,972 --> 00:00:17,684
<i>Have you run out of tricks</i>
<i>to escape from this?</i>

5
00:00:18,852 --> 00:00:20,270
<i>Billy, you're right.</i>

6
00:00:21,229 --> 00:00:22,814
<i>I wronged you.</i>

7
00:00:22,897 --> 00:00:24,941
<i>I wronged your family too.</i>

8
00:00:29,070 --> 00:00:30,363
<i>I did it because you stole from me.</i>

9
00:00:30,447 --> 00:00:32,115
<i>I never stole anything from you.</i>

10
00:00:32,699 --> 00:00:34,576
<i>You tore my family apart, Billy.</i>

11
00:00:34,659 --> 00:00:37,328
<i>Because you stole my father from us.</i>

12
00:00:37,412 --> 00:00:38,496
<i>Billy?</i>

13
00:00:42,834 --> 00:00:45,462
<i>Bea? Sweetheart?</i>

14
00:00:55,055 --> 00:00:57,515
[DOCTOR] <i>Enrico has entered</i>
<i>the advanced stage of heart failure,</i>

15
00:00:57,599 --> 00:01:00,143
<i>and this has been developing</i>
<i>for quite some time.</i>

16
00:01:00,226 --> 00:01:02,270
<i>His arteries are blocked,</i>

17
00:01:02,353 --> 00:01:04,606
<i>leading to ischemic heart disease.</i>

18
00:01:04,689 --> 00:01:09,444
<i>His condition has been</i>
<i>further worsened by his diabetes.</i>

19
00:01:10,528 --> 00:01:12,155
<i>Why didn't you tell us?</i>

20
00:01:13,281 --> 00:01:15,575
<i>I didn't tell you because</i>

21
00:01:16,409 --> 00:01:20,580
<i>I didn't want you to think</i>
<i>that was the reason</i>

22
00:01:20,663 --> 00:01:22,457
<i>I'm asking for your forgiveness.</i>

23
00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:27,962
<i>I just want to spend my remaining days…</i>

24
00:01:28,046 --> 00:01:31,299
[MACHINE BEEPING STEADILY]

25
00:01:31,382 --> 00:01:32,884
<i>…with you.</i>

26
00:01:34,135 --> 00:01:38,848
<i>I want us to patch things up</i>
<i>and be a family.</i>

27
00:01:38,932 --> 00:01:41,226
<i>That is all I want.</i>

28
00:01:41,309 --> 00:01:45,313
[MARIELA] <i>Maybe he could get us</i>
<i>out of here then.</i>

29
00:01:45,396 --> 00:01:48,274
<i>That was always the plan.</i>

30
00:01:50,902 --> 00:01:56,282
<i>If we exploit their kindness,</i>
<i>we can get out of here.</i>

31
00:01:57,075 --> 00:01:58,368
<i>Then…</i>

32
00:02:01,121 --> 00:02:03,081
<i>we're going to destroy them again.</i>

33
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:10,046
<i>We're going to destroy their family.</i>

34
00:02:10,130 --> 00:02:12,882
<i>Then we'll get your father back.</i>

35
00:02:14,342 --> 00:02:15,593
<i>After that,</i>

36
00:02:16,845 --> 00:02:18,847
<i>our family will be together again.</i>

37
00:02:25,478 --> 00:02:28,314
<i>If we can get your father to side with us,</i>

38
00:02:29,899 --> 00:02:31,609
<i>we can definitely get out of here.</i>

39
00:02:32,861 --> 00:02:35,196
<i>Even if Billy is against it.</i>

40
00:02:41,202 --> 00:02:42,620
<i>Listen, Bea.</i>

41
00:02:45,206 --> 00:02:47,584
<i>I need you to do something.</i>

42
00:02:48,585 --> 00:02:53,089
<i>Find out how your father's doing.</i>

43
00:03:05,727 --> 00:03:07,228
- Pa.
- Hm?

44
00:03:07,312 --> 00:03:08,479
Time to take your medicine.

45
00:03:08,563 --> 00:03:10,356
What about you? Did you take yours?

46
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:12,191
Pa, see? Got mine ready.

47
00:03:12,275 --> 00:03:14,777
- Okay. Together, then?
- [OLIVER] Here. Okay.

48
00:03:16,112 --> 00:03:18,323
- Cheers. Mm.
- Cheers!

49
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:24,495
There, all done.

50
00:03:25,163 --> 00:03:26,456
- Um… Pa?
- Mm?

51
00:03:26,539 --> 00:03:29,459
- I'm going back to school tomorrow.
- Right.

52
00:03:29,542 --> 00:03:32,128
How about you?
When are you going back to work?

53
00:03:32,211 --> 00:03:33,296
Next week.

54
00:03:34,547 --> 00:03:35,632
All right, Pa.

55
00:03:36,883 --> 00:03:37,842
You should go to sleep.

56
00:03:39,093 --> 00:03:40,595
I just need to finish this.

57
00:03:40,678 --> 00:03:42,847
- [OLIVER] Time for bed.
- Huh? Are you sleepy?

58
00:03:42,931 --> 00:03:45,433
- Let's go to sleep.
- Go on. You're the one who needs sleep.

59
00:03:45,516 --> 00:03:46,517
- Okay.
- [CHUCKLES]

60
00:03:46,601 --> 00:03:48,144
- Good night.
- Let me finish this.

61
00:03:48,228 --> 00:03:49,354
Okay, love you.

62
00:03:49,437 --> 00:03:50,772
- Good night. Love you.
- Yes, okay.

63
00:03:50,855 --> 00:03:53,691
- Mwah! Good night.
- Mm! Good night.

64
00:03:53,775 --> 00:03:55,735
[GRUNTS, GIGGLES] No!

65
00:03:57,278 --> 00:03:59,322
Good night to you, my beautiful sister.

66
00:03:59,405 --> 00:04:01,032
- Good night.
- [SMOOCHES] Go on to sleep.

67
00:04:01,115 --> 00:04:02,408
Did you say good night to Dad?

68
00:04:02,492 --> 00:04:05,620
- Yeah. Good night! Bye, guys!
- Get some rest.

69
00:04:05,703 --> 00:04:06,996
- Dad? Um…
- Hmm?

70
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:10,708
You have a follow-up consultation
with the doctor tomorrow.

71
00:04:10,792 --> 00:04:12,085
That's right.

72
00:04:12,669 --> 00:04:16,798
Don't force yourself
to go back to work too soon.

73
00:04:17,632 --> 00:04:21,761
The doctor said the procedure
was only minimally invasive,

74
00:04:21,844 --> 00:04:25,306
so I feel like I'll be fine by next week.

75
00:04:25,390 --> 00:04:26,641
Um…

76
00:04:27,475 --> 00:04:30,603
Sweetheart, there's something
I need to tell you.

77
00:04:31,813 --> 00:04:32,897
What is it?

78
00:04:32,981 --> 00:04:36,484
I want to go visit
Bea and Mariela for a bit.

79
00:04:37,735 --> 00:04:38,778
Mm-hmm.

80
00:04:40,863 --> 00:04:45,743
That's okay. I know you have
responsibilities to them too.

81
00:04:46,494 --> 00:04:47,704
Thank you, sweetie.

82
00:04:48,413 --> 00:04:49,289
Okay.

83
00:04:49,956 --> 00:04:52,041
- Get some rest.
- Good night.

84
00:04:52,125 --> 00:04:57,463
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING, THEN FADES]

85
00:04:57,547 --> 00:05:04,262
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

86
00:05:41,591 --> 00:05:43,426
[PAPERS RUSTLING]

87
00:05:45,219 --> 00:05:47,430
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

88
00:05:50,058 --> 00:05:52,268
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

89
00:05:55,313 --> 00:05:57,857
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

90
00:06:07,950 --> 00:06:09,243
[PHONE CHIMES]

91
00:06:12,371 --> 00:06:16,626
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

92
00:06:16,709 --> 00:06:20,922
- HOW ARE YOU, DUDE?
- I'M OKAY, JUST DOING SOME PAPERWORK.

93
00:06:21,005 --> 00:06:24,175
- ARE YOU GOING TO THE BAR LATER?
- I'LL SEE IF I HAVE TIME.

94
00:06:24,258 --> 00:06:25,551
Dude, come on.

95
00:06:26,761 --> 00:06:28,846
I know that your hospital bills
are piling up.

96
00:06:29,555 --> 00:06:31,557
Please, let me help.

97
00:06:32,266 --> 00:06:33,226
Just a little.

98
00:06:35,103 --> 00:06:37,313
The beer and pizza are more than enough.

99
00:06:37,396 --> 00:06:39,315
- [GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]
- [JORDAN SIGHS]

100
00:06:39,398 --> 00:06:41,984
Dude, it's me, okay?

101
00:06:42,068 --> 00:06:44,612
It's me. We're friends, remember?

102
00:06:44,695 --> 00:06:47,240
Remember me, Jordan, your best friend?

103
00:06:51,452 --> 00:06:53,121
Of course we got each other's backs.

104
00:06:53,204 --> 00:06:57,250
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

105
00:06:57,333 --> 00:06:59,043
- [BOTTLE THUDS]
- Besides,

106
00:06:59,627 --> 00:07:01,170
my bar is doing great.

107
00:07:01,838 --> 00:07:05,341
Thanks to Val and the video she posted.

108
00:07:05,424 --> 00:07:06,259
Mm-hmm.

109
00:07:06,342 --> 00:07:07,635
It has 2 million views already.

110
00:07:08,261 --> 00:07:09,137
[BILLY] Wow.

111
00:07:09,804 --> 00:07:11,848
Jade & Jude's is trending right now.

112
00:07:13,850 --> 00:07:15,184
I'm happy for you.

113
00:07:17,437 --> 00:07:18,479
Thanks, dude.

114
00:07:19,272 --> 00:07:20,731
But enough about me.

115
00:07:21,941 --> 00:07:23,901
What about you? How's your dad?

116
00:07:24,610 --> 00:07:25,820
He's doing okay.

117
00:07:26,487 --> 00:07:28,531
Sorry I was late.

118
00:07:28,614 --> 00:07:31,409
I wasn't able to check on him personally.

119
00:07:31,993 --> 00:07:35,371
And… what about Bea?

120
00:07:35,455 --> 00:07:40,001
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

121
00:07:40,084 --> 00:07:43,087
I still can't believe that
she's my sister.

122
00:07:44,172 --> 00:07:47,133
Well, at least, your question
has been answered.

123
00:07:48,259 --> 00:07:50,344
We finally know why Bea is mad at you.

124
00:07:50,428 --> 00:07:52,638
Why she did everything
that she did to you,

125
00:07:52,722 --> 00:07:56,100
to LoveList, and to your family…

126
00:07:56,184 --> 00:07:57,894
Because she was hurt?

127
00:08:01,898 --> 00:08:03,649
Can you forgive her?

128
00:08:03,733 --> 00:08:08,613
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

129
00:08:08,696 --> 00:08:10,031
I'd understand if you can't.

130
00:08:11,908 --> 00:08:13,784
You were both hurt.

131
00:08:14,535 --> 00:08:16,078
But in your case,

132
00:08:16,162 --> 00:08:19,248
you chose to rise up from that experience.

133
00:08:19,999 --> 00:08:21,250
Dude, you…

134
00:08:21,334 --> 00:08:22,668
You used that pain.

135
00:08:24,253 --> 00:08:25,463
Made it something good.

136
00:08:26,047 --> 00:08:27,089
It made you

137
00:08:27,924 --> 00:08:29,133
an amazing person.

138
00:08:30,301 --> 00:08:31,594
Bea had the same choice,

139
00:08:32,303 --> 00:08:34,180
but that's not what she did.

140
00:08:34,764 --> 00:08:36,766
She ruined herself

141
00:08:37,391 --> 00:08:40,520
and tried to ruin the lives of others.

142
00:08:42,271 --> 00:08:46,776
I don't know if she's sincerely
asking for forgiveness.

143
00:08:46,859 --> 00:08:50,112
She might be planning something
against us again.

144
00:08:53,699 --> 00:08:55,201
You can go now.

145
00:08:55,284 --> 00:08:57,995
I know you're busy at the bar.
Just come back some other day.

146
00:08:58,621 --> 00:09:00,081
Thank you for all this.

147
00:09:00,873 --> 00:09:01,874
Are you sure?

148
00:09:03,167 --> 00:09:04,752
Okay. Anytime.

149
00:09:05,336 --> 00:09:10,049
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

150
00:09:18,808 --> 00:09:21,102
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

151
00:09:21,686 --> 00:09:23,646
- I'll get the motorcycle.
- Okay, you know what to do.

152
00:09:24,230 --> 00:09:25,439
[CALOY] Get some clothes for us.

153
00:09:25,523 --> 00:09:30,903
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

154
00:09:30,987 --> 00:09:32,238
[CALOY GRUNTS]

155
00:09:34,699 --> 00:09:36,826
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE STARTS]

156
00:09:36,909 --> 00:09:41,497
- [TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [MOTORCYCLE ENGINE REVVING]

157
00:09:41,581 --> 00:09:43,165
[MUSIC FADES]

158
00:09:45,001 --> 00:09:52,008
- [BROODING MUSIC PLAYING]
- [DOG BARKING IN DISTANCE]

159
00:10:02,184 --> 00:10:03,769
So, this is their house?

160
00:10:03,853 --> 00:10:04,937
Where are they?

161
00:10:05,646 --> 00:10:06,772
I don't know.

162
00:10:08,691 --> 00:10:10,234
Yes, it's vacant.

163
00:10:10,318 --> 00:10:12,153
You can rent it for 6,000 pesos.

164
00:10:12,236 --> 00:10:13,946
- Come on now. It's for you.
- Hey!

165
00:10:14,030 --> 00:10:15,740
Hey! Didn't you hear me call you?!

166
00:10:15,823 --> 00:10:18,826
- Where are Ms. Mariela and Bea?
- Why?! Who are you?!

167
00:10:18,909 --> 00:10:20,161
- Who am I?
- [WHIMPERS]

168
00:10:20,244 --> 00:10:22,455
Answer my question,
or I'll smash your face with this.

169
00:10:22,538 --> 00:10:25,124
- [CALOY] Where are they?!
- [CRISELDA] I don't know!

170
00:10:27,251 --> 00:10:28,210
I kicked them out.

171
00:10:28,294 --> 00:10:30,046
- I don't care where they are.
- [DINO] Go away!

172
00:10:30,129 --> 00:10:31,756
- You don't care, huh?
- [DINO] Go! Leave!

173
00:10:31,839 --> 00:10:34,091
I said go away. Stop being nosy.

174
00:10:34,175 --> 00:10:36,093
- Is her daughter with her?
- [DINO] Leave!

175
00:10:36,177 --> 00:10:38,346
- Answer me!
- Why are you looking for them?

176
00:10:38,429 --> 00:10:39,639
Do they owe you money?

177
00:10:39,722 --> 00:10:40,931
It's none of your business!

178
00:10:42,016 --> 00:10:43,059
You're useless!

179
00:10:43,142 --> 00:10:44,101
Let's go.

180
00:10:44,185 --> 00:10:45,770
[CRISELDA WHIMPERS]

181
00:10:45,853 --> 00:10:47,146
[DINO] Come on!

182
00:10:47,229 --> 00:10:49,106
- [LOUD THUD]
- [CRISELDA] My goodness!

183
00:10:51,776 --> 00:10:54,070
You can't stay here long, okay?
I'll get in trouble.

184
00:10:55,446 --> 00:10:57,156
Caloy said you can help us.

185
00:10:57,239 --> 00:10:59,325
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

186
00:10:59,408 --> 00:11:02,119
Your girlfriend also asked for my help.

187
00:11:02,703 --> 00:11:04,914
My girlfriend? You mean Bea?

188
00:11:04,997 --> 00:11:08,125
Yes, I met with her the other week.

189
00:11:08,209 --> 00:11:10,711
She asked me to make a fake passport
for her and her mom.

190
00:11:10,795 --> 00:11:12,254
Why? What for?

191
00:11:12,338 --> 00:11:13,339
Don't you know?

192
00:11:14,298 --> 00:11:15,674
They're in jail.

193
00:11:16,759 --> 00:11:18,094
Here, look.

194
00:11:18,177 --> 00:11:20,179
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

195
00:11:23,849 --> 00:11:29,939
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

196
00:11:38,489 --> 00:11:40,408
They won't hurt you anymore.

197
00:11:40,491 --> 00:11:42,243
They won't dare.

198
00:11:43,452 --> 00:11:46,997
So, any update on your father?

199
00:11:48,290 --> 00:11:49,542
Nothing yet, Ma.

200
00:11:51,085 --> 00:11:52,545
What if he died?

201
00:11:53,170 --> 00:11:55,548
Or worse, what if he's still alive

202
00:11:55,631 --> 00:11:58,843
but his bastard child brainwashed him

203
00:11:58,926 --> 00:12:00,594
into forgetting about us?

204
00:12:03,806 --> 00:12:06,517
Mercado, you two have visitors.

205
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:11,981
We have visitors? Who are they?

206
00:12:12,565 --> 00:12:15,359
Benilda Cariño and Enrico Dominguez.

207
00:12:15,443 --> 00:12:22,241
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

208
00:12:23,451 --> 00:12:26,787
[METAL GATE RATTLING]

209
00:12:28,539 --> 00:12:31,167
Ma, listen to me.

210
00:12:32,877 --> 00:12:34,670
I need you to do something.

211
00:12:34,753 --> 00:12:39,341
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

212
00:12:48,434 --> 00:12:52,771
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

213
00:12:53,355 --> 00:12:55,733
- Ma! Ma! Ma! Ma!
- [ANGRY GRUNT]

214
00:12:55,816 --> 00:12:58,194
I already erased you from my life

215
00:12:58,277 --> 00:13:02,072
and we're no longer using your surname.

216
00:13:02,656 --> 00:13:07,244
I thought it would help me
forget how much you've hurt me!

217
00:13:07,328 --> 00:13:12,041
But every time I think about how
someone stole you from me…

218
00:13:12,124 --> 00:13:13,083
Ma…

219
00:13:13,167 --> 00:13:16,253
…the pain and anger come back!

220
00:13:16,337 --> 00:13:17,213
[BEA] Ma…

221
00:13:17,296 --> 00:13:18,797
I tried to take my own life.

222
00:13:20,132 --> 00:13:22,176
And because of that,
our house burned down.

223
00:13:22,801 --> 00:13:24,220
It's why Abigail died!

224
00:13:24,303 --> 00:13:26,972
- Abigail died because of you!
- Ma! Ma!

225
00:13:27,056 --> 00:13:29,016
- Dad, let's go.
- It's all your fault, Enrico!

226
00:13:29,099 --> 00:13:30,392
- Let's go.
- Calm down.

227
00:13:30,476 --> 00:13:32,520
[ENRICO] Bea, let's talk calmly.

228
00:13:32,603 --> 00:13:33,979
Stay out of this!

229
00:13:34,063 --> 00:13:35,981
You're just his mistress's daughter.

230
00:13:36,065 --> 00:13:40,152
[BEA] Ma, don't get mad at Billy.

231
00:13:40,736 --> 00:13:42,154
Why are you defending her?

232
00:13:43,072 --> 00:13:44,573
No, it's not that.

233
00:13:44,657 --> 00:13:46,909
But we were wrong.
Billy didn't take anything from us.

234
00:13:46,992 --> 00:13:48,285
She has nothing to do with all this.

235
00:13:48,369 --> 00:13:51,789
We shouldn't have taken out
our anger on her.

236
00:13:51,872 --> 00:13:54,625
In fact, you should apologize to Billy.

237
00:13:54,708 --> 00:14:00,631
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

238
00:14:06,929 --> 00:14:09,098
[MUSIC FADES]

239
00:14:13,102 --> 00:14:16,814
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

240
00:14:16,897 --> 00:14:17,856
Dear…

241
00:14:20,776 --> 00:14:23,070
Can you forgive your sister?

242
00:14:23,153 --> 00:14:28,284
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

243
00:14:34,665 --> 00:14:37,293
[BIRDS CHIRPING IN DISTANCE]

244
00:14:37,376 --> 00:14:39,962
Any update on 202 Capital Group?

245
00:14:40,045 --> 00:14:42,339
Have they read our proposal?

246
00:14:42,423 --> 00:14:44,592
Um… Chief, they passed.

247
00:14:44,675 --> 00:14:47,553
They said the company
is still too volatile

248
00:14:47,636 --> 00:14:51,098
for a large-scale
expansion investment right now.

249
00:14:51,891 --> 00:14:56,979
As for Kayrova Tech Holdings,
they haven't responded yet.

250
00:14:57,062 --> 00:14:59,857
RCDV is a bit hesitant.

251
00:14:59,940 --> 00:15:02,067
Hesitant because?

252
00:15:04,278 --> 00:15:08,657
We ran another brand trust
and credibility scan.

253
00:15:09,241 --> 00:15:12,411
Investment sentiment dropped 18 percent

254
00:15:12,494 --> 00:15:15,080
after the hacking incident.

255
00:15:15,748 --> 00:15:18,792
Then, another 12

256
00:15:19,335 --> 00:15:23,130
after the news about the fire
at Billy's house broke out.

257
00:15:25,424 --> 00:15:28,719
They check on those things,
including the fire?

258
00:15:29,386 --> 00:15:31,889
Well, Billy is the face of LoveList,

259
00:15:32,473 --> 00:15:37,478
so even her personal issues
can affect the company.

260
00:15:38,479 --> 00:15:40,898
Public perception is everywhere now.

261
00:15:41,774 --> 00:15:44,985
And negative association
attached to LoveList

262
00:15:45,069 --> 00:15:51,533
are mostly security risk, stability, and…

263
00:15:53,494 --> 00:15:55,162
Leadership controversy.

264
00:15:57,206 --> 00:15:58,290
[WHISPERS] Yeah.

265
00:15:59,541 --> 00:16:04,964
Actually, I happen to know
a potential investor.

266
00:16:08,384 --> 00:16:13,347
She just wants to know who
burned down your house.

267
00:16:16,141 --> 00:16:17,768
Her main concern is:

268
00:16:17,851 --> 00:16:21,271
if someone was willing
to target you personally,

269
00:16:21,355 --> 00:16:26,026
what's stopping them from
targeting LoveList next?

270
00:16:26,110 --> 00:16:31,991
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

271
00:16:32,074 --> 00:16:34,868
Sorry, but that's a valid concern

272
00:16:34,952 --> 00:16:37,121
from a risk assessment standpoint, right?

273
00:16:38,038 --> 00:16:38,998
Right, Jordan?

274
00:16:40,207 --> 00:16:43,502
[CHARM] Guys, our issues
are way too public.

275
00:16:43,585 --> 00:16:47,423
People online are treating LoveList
like we're on a reality show.

276
00:16:49,008 --> 00:16:52,469
Val and Marj are doing
damage control right now

277
00:16:52,553 --> 00:16:56,056
to clean up your name online.

278
00:16:56,140 --> 00:16:59,393
I just doubt it'll work, though.

279
00:16:59,476 --> 00:17:03,147
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

280
00:17:03,230 --> 00:17:04,940
Okay, guys, that's enough.

281
00:17:05,607 --> 00:17:06,692
Let's move on.

282
00:17:07,443 --> 00:17:10,279
Let's hear some solutions.

283
00:17:10,904 --> 00:17:12,031
Can we?

284
00:17:13,699 --> 00:17:16,410
I get the numbers, I get the optics.

285
00:17:16,493 --> 00:17:19,455
But if we start operating out of fear,

286
00:17:19,538 --> 00:17:23,208
then we're done
before we even launch globally.

287
00:17:23,292 --> 00:17:26,378
Jordan's right.
What we need is a solution.

288
00:17:26,462 --> 00:17:28,547
A solution that actually works.

289
00:17:30,340 --> 00:17:32,301
- Charm.
- Yes, chief?

290
00:17:32,384 --> 00:17:33,761
What still works for us?

291
00:17:35,304 --> 00:17:37,014
Um…

292
00:17:37,097 --> 00:17:40,768
The success stories of users. Right?

293
00:17:40,851 --> 00:17:41,852
[MORRIE] Yes, chief.

294
00:17:41,935 --> 00:17:46,065
Our engagement is highest
when we feature real couples.

295
00:17:46,148 --> 00:17:48,692
- Okay, then. Let's focus on that.
- [CHARM] Okay.

296
00:17:48,776 --> 00:17:53,947
Let's remind them why
they trusted LoveList in the first place.

297
00:17:54,031 --> 00:17:56,200
We'll launch something bigger.

298
00:17:56,283 --> 00:17:59,328
Media coverage, real couples,
success stories.

299
00:17:59,411 --> 00:18:01,038
If trust is the issue here,

300
00:18:01,121 --> 00:18:03,373
then we'll rebuild that trust publicly.

301
00:18:04,249 --> 00:18:06,335
That's a good strategy.

302
00:18:06,418 --> 00:18:13,217
But with our negative image right now,
sponsors might be hard to find.

303
00:18:13,300 --> 00:18:16,553
["TABLA TAYO" BY FANA PLAYING]

304
00:18:16,637 --> 00:18:18,847
Then what's your idea, Toni?

305
00:18:18,931 --> 00:18:24,353
["TABLA TAYO" CONTINUES]

306
00:18:24,436 --> 00:18:26,230
Any suggestions?

307
00:18:26,313 --> 00:18:32,444
["TABLA TAYO" CONTINUES]

308
00:18:38,283 --> 00:18:39,326
[INHALES DEEPLY]

309
00:18:39,409 --> 00:18:41,161
Let's regroup tomorrow morning.

310
00:18:42,162 --> 00:18:44,414
And I want real solutions,

311
00:18:44,498 --> 00:18:46,959
not just problems dumped on me.

312
00:18:47,042 --> 00:18:48,877
But, Billy, tomorrow…

313
00:18:48,961 --> 00:18:50,295
tomorrow is Saturday.

314
00:18:50,379 --> 00:18:52,840
Yani and I have plans.

315
00:18:53,715 --> 00:18:57,553
Plus, it's Ralph's mom's birthday.

316
00:18:59,680 --> 00:19:01,181
[MORRIE] I'm watching a concert.

317
00:19:01,265 --> 00:19:03,600
I already bought a ticket.

318
00:19:03,684 --> 00:19:10,232
[GLUM MUSIC PLAYING]

319
00:19:10,315 --> 00:19:11,441
What?

320
00:19:11,525 --> 00:19:17,197
[GLUM MUSIC CONTINUES]

321
00:19:18,657 --> 00:19:20,367
I know it's the weekend.

322
00:19:21,076 --> 00:19:23,871
But you can file an offset, right?

323
00:19:25,372 --> 00:19:26,456
Right?

324
00:19:28,333 --> 00:19:29,209
[VOICE TREMBLES] Guys.

325
00:19:30,961 --> 00:19:34,173
The company is
literally bleeding right now.

326
00:19:34,256 --> 00:19:38,802
[GLUM MUSIC CONTINUES]

327
00:19:38,886 --> 00:19:41,138
Where's your commitment to your work?

328
00:19:41,221 --> 00:19:46,560
[GLUM MUSIC CONTINUES]

329
00:19:48,979 --> 00:19:50,647
Dude, sorry.

330
00:19:51,690 --> 00:19:53,734
I have a podcast guesting
tomorrow morning,

331
00:19:53,817 --> 00:19:57,070
but after that, I'm free all day.

332
00:19:57,154 --> 00:19:58,989
Maybe we can do a Zoom meeting?

333
00:20:00,073 --> 00:20:02,326
- Guys, how's your Saturday?
- [BLAIRE] I'm free.

334
00:20:02,409 --> 00:20:03,911
- Okay.
- No, it's fine.

335
00:20:03,994 --> 00:20:06,079
- Sunday?
- No. I'll see you Monday.

336
00:20:06,163 --> 00:20:07,122
Billy?

337
00:20:07,206 --> 00:20:12,961
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

338
00:20:22,179 --> 00:20:24,181
[KAREN] <i>Hey, everyone! We're--</i>

339
00:20:25,224 --> 00:20:26,183
[DINO] <i>Did you miss me?</i>

340
00:20:26,266 --> 00:20:28,602
<i>Maybe you just need a break.</i>
<i>Come to my gig tonight.</i>

341
00:20:28,685 --> 00:20:32,231
<i>With everything on my plate right now,</i>
<i>you want me to come to your gig?</i>

342
00:20:32,314 --> 00:20:37,361
<i>They said your check bounced for the</i>
<i>down payment on the house rebuild.</i>

343
00:20:37,444 --> 00:20:39,613
<i>- I texted you the other day--</i>
<i>- You only texted me, Blaire!</i>

344
00:20:39,696 --> 00:20:41,365
<i>You should've called me!</i>

345
00:20:41,448 --> 00:20:43,367
<i>We still have to come up</i>
<i>with something to present Billy.</i>

346
00:20:43,450 --> 00:20:46,536
[BILLY] <i>What I need to be okay</i>
<i>are results.</i>

347
00:20:46,620 --> 00:20:48,330
<i>Ideas to help the company.</i>

348
00:20:48,413 --> 00:20:51,875
<i>But everywhere I go,</i>
<i>all I hear about are problems!</i>

349
00:20:51,959 --> 00:20:54,962
<i>I'll make these bastards pay.</i>

350
00:20:55,045 --> 00:20:58,590
<i>♪ Do you know when I found you</i>
<i>Everything changed? ♪</i>

351
00:20:58,674 --> 00:21:01,426
<i>♪ Wherever I go ♪</i>

352
00:21:02,594 --> 00:21:04,805
<i>Just withdraw the case</i>
<i>against my mother.</i>

353
00:21:04,888 --> 00:21:05,806
<i>Please, Billy. Please.</i>

354
00:21:05,889 --> 00:21:07,474
<i>Have mercy on my mother. Please.</i>

355
00:21:07,557 --> 00:21:08,976
<i>If you were in my position,</i>

356
00:21:09,059 --> 00:21:13,605
<i>and your family had almost died</i>
<i>because of someone,</i>

357
00:21:13,689 --> 00:21:15,482
<i>would you really let her walk free?</i>

358
00:21:15,565 --> 00:21:18,986
- [INMATE] <i>She's a lost cause!</i>
<i>- Let's see who's really the lost cause!</i>

359
00:21:19,069 --> 00:21:22,864
[INMATES GRUNTING,
SCREAMING]
